.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-key 1  "key "
.SH NAME
dotman\-key \- Create or import the age identity that decrypts encrypted files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman key\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create or import the age identity that decrypts encrypted files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dotman\-key\-init(1)
Generate an age identity and add its recipient to .dotman.toml
.TP
dotman\-key\-import(1)
Copy an existing age identity into place and check that its recipient is listed
